From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Trey Moen <trey@moen.ai>
Date: Mon, 15 Jun 2026 20:30:00 +0000
Subject: clk: qcom: camcc-sdm845: match legacy titan_top GDSC wait timing

The legacy AGNOS 4.9 kernel programs the titan_top GDSC with CLK_DIS_WAIT=0xF
and EN_FEW_WAIT=2 (read live from GDSCR 0xad0b134 = 0x0022F001). Mainline's gdsc
driver uses its defaults (CLK_DIS_WAIT=2, EN_FEW_WAIT=8). The camera sensor I2C
front-end is gated by the TITAN_TOP config power domain; align the wait timing
with the known-good legacy value as part of the camera bring-up.
---
diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/camcc-sdm845.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/camcc-sdm845.c
index cf60e8dd2..38321c17e 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/camcc-sdm845.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/camcc-sdm845.c
@@ -1591,6 +1591,9 @@ static struct gdsc titan_top_gdsc = {
 	},
 	.flags = POLL_CFG_GDSCR,
 	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
+	/* TITAN_TOP config-domain ramp the sensor I2C front-end depends on */
+	.en_few_wait_val = 0x2,
+	.clk_dis_wait_val = 0xf,
 };
 
 static struct clk_regmap *cam_cc_sdm845_clocks[] = {
-- 
2.43.0
